# DTF tier manifest: suffix-format-index-paths  (#2589)
# Profile-set: filesystem / single. The advertised download URL is computed at
# metadata-serve time from the artifact's stored path; this is storage-agnostic
# and the download route resolves by filename suffix, so the default filesystem
# overlay exercises it fully.
#
# WHAT IT GUARDS (#2589, follow-up to #2587/#2754):
#   The suffix-resolved formats whose JSON metadata advertises an EXPLICIT,
#   directly-followed download URL — RubyGems (gem_info/versions `gem_uri`),
#   Ansible Galaxy (`download_url`) and Puppet Forge (`file_uri`) — reconstruct
#   that URL from the package coordinates `{name}(-{version}).ext`. A package
#   pushed through the generic (bare-path) upload flow is stored at an arbitrary
#   path whose basename need NOT equal the reconstructed filename, so the
#   advertised URL pointed at a path the suffix-resolving download route (the
#   #2587 exact-path fallback) could never serve -> the client follows the
#   advertised link and 404s even though the artifact is present. This is the
#   RPM `primary.xml` `<location>` bug (#2587) generalized to these formats: the
#   fix advertises the artifact's actual stored basename.
#
# Discriminating oracle (oracle.sh): for each format, generic (bare-path)
# chunked-upload an artifact at a path whose basename differs from the canonical
# `{name}(-{version}).ext`, read the SERVED metadata document, extract the
# advertised download URL VERBATIM, and GET it.
#   Fixed (#2589): the advertised URL carries the real stored basename -> 200.
#   Pre-#2589:     the advertised URL is the reconstructed canonical filename,
#                  which the bare-path artifact is not stored under -> 404 -> FAIL.
# A companion assertion confirms the canonical reconstructed path (what a
# pre-fix build would have advertised) 404s, pinning that the advertised URL and
# the served route are the SAME object only on the fixed build.
#
# RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED=false: the oracle drives admin login + three generic
# chunked uploads (session + chunk + complete) + metadata/download GETs
# back-to-back.
PROFILES="storage.filesystem"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
